      [
        "Performance Features",
        "1. High vacuum degree (0.09～0.098 MPa), low filter‑cake moisture.\n2. Solid content of filtrate is less than 50 ppm. Filtrate can be reused repeatedly to reduce discharge.\n3. Energy consumption is reduced by more than 90% compared with traditional filtration equipment, featuring low energy consumption and low operating cost.\n4. Filter‑cake washing function is added compared with conventional ceramic filters, suitable for materials requiring washing.\n5. Controlled by PLC, microcomputer and automatic valves, with high automation and reduced labor intensity.\n6. Compact structure, small footprint, convenient installation and maintenance.\n7. Advanced liquid‑discharge system, suitable for any working conditions.",
        "",
        "",
        "",
        "",
        ""
      ],
      [
        "Working Principle",
        "Suction zone: During operation, the filter plate immersed in slurry adsorbs a layer of filter cake on its surface under capillary action combined with vacuum pressure. Filtrate passes through the filter plate, enters the distribution valve and flows to the discharge tank.\n\nWashing zone: After the filter cake rotates out of the slurry tank, spray washing is applied to the filter cake.\n\nDrying zone: The filter cake continues to be dewatered under high vacuum force.\n\nDischarging zone: Under non‑vacuum condition, the scraper automatically discharges the filter cake.\n\nBackwashing: Industrial water or filtrate enters the ceramic plate through the distribution valve and cleans it from inside to outside, removing blocked micropores. After one service cycle of the ceramic plate, ultrasonic cleaning combined with low‑concentration acid is adopted to maintain efficient performance of the ceramic plate.",
        "",
        "",
